Ringer licensing

Ringer's own code is MIT (see LICENSE). That covers plugin/, engine/, docs/ and the top-level files.

Five other projects are vendored here, each with its full upstream history, in its own directory.
They are not modified by Ringer and each keeps its own licence file:

  iphone-connect/   Badr Said Emil          MIT
  omyphone/         Boyidzham               MIT
  phone-airplay/    Adam Moussa Ali         MIT
  sidecar/          Omarchy Sidecar contributors   MIT
  blueferry/        Erik Bourget and others GPL-2.0-only

The MIT licence at the top level does not apply to those directories. blueferry/ is GPL-2.0-only and
is kept as a separate directory, not merged into Ringer's code.

Ringer's own code does not copy from the vendored projects. plugin/bin/ringer calls the iphone-connect
backend as an external command.

The engine imports pymobiledevice3 (GPL-3.0, by doronz88). It is not included in this repository: install
it separately. MIT is compatible with the GPL, so Ringer's source can be distributed under MIT, but
anyone who combines it with pymobiledevice3 is bound by that library's GPL-3.0 terms for the combination.
